%% Session Lifecycle — What happens at session start and session close

flowchart TD
    START([Session begins]) --> WALK[Atlas walks tasks/open/ and tasks/in-progress/]
    WALK --> REPORT[Atlas reports status to user]
    REPORT --> BLOCKED{Blocked tasks?}
    BLOCKED -->|Yes| FLAG[Surface blockers prominently]
    BLOCKED -->|No| WORK
    FLAG --> WORK[Normal session work begins]

    WORK --> DELEGATE[Atlas delegates to agents]
    DELEGATE --> CREATE_TASK{Work spans sessions?}
    CREATE_TASK -->|Yes| TASK[Create task in tasks/open/]
    CREATE_TASK -->|No| DIRECT[Agent executes directly]
    TASK --> AGENT_WORK[Agent works on task]
    DIRECT --> AGENT_WORK

    AGENT_WORK --> JOURNAL{Durable insight?}
    JOURNAL -->|Yes| WRITE_JOURNAL[Write journal entry]
    JOURNAL -->|No| CONTINUE
    WRITE_JOURNAL --> CONTINUE[Continue or close]

    CONTINUE --> CLOSE([User signals session end])
    CLOSE --> LOG[Atlas writes session log]
    LOG --> UPDATE_TASKS[Update all tasks touched]
    UPDATE_TASKS --> UPDATE_INDEX[Update Session Logs/INDEX.md]
    UPDATE_INDEX --> CONFIRM[Confirm to user: Session logged]
